{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles","id":1514463,"title":"Gargoyles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-10T06:39:02-07:00","id":1514463,"title":"Gargoyles","content":"Hello guys, I was reading about gargoyles in Requiem, and in Danse Macabre says the knowledge to create gargoyles is quite widespread, I founded it quite strange because the population of gargoyles shoulder be really higher (why trust just in ghouls to protect your haven if you can have a Gargoyles too). Did I missed something? Gargoyles never come up in games I played, so I wanted to know how usually things work in your games.<br /> <br /> I don't usually post anything, so if I did something wrong, just let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T07:24:39-07:00","id":1514468,"title":"","content":"I think it's because they didn't make the jump to 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T09:07:03-07:00","id":1514469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles#post1514463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys, I was reading about gargoyles in Requiem, and in Danse Macabre says the knowledge to create gargoyles is quite widespread, I founded it quite strange because the population of gargoyles shoulder be really higher (why trust just in ghouls to protect your haven if you can have a Gargoyles too). Did I missed something? Gargoyles never come up in games I played, so I wanted to know how usually things work in your games.<br /> <br /> I don't usually post anything, so if I did something wrong, just let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, i'd say &quot;quite widespread&quot; is a very vague and loose definition, in that it can go from &quot;as common as ghouls&quot; (as you kind of compared them) to &quot;almost as numerous as users of Cruac, Theban Sorcery or Dragon's Coils&quot; to anywhere within those extremes or beyond them.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, the greater issue is that back in the corebook gargoyles were nothing beyond one antagonist type and its vague, hermetic sort of fluff blurb, meaning that players and STs had pretty much <i><b>nothing</b></i> to go on with for almost 7 years before Danse Macabre came out and we got a whole book chapter and some mechanics on them for the first time, ever.<br /> <br /> And then 2nd edition came out - and i have no idea whatsoever of how Danse Macabre's material on gargoyles is applicable or not for 2nd ed. an uncertainty that i suspect is far from uncommon for a huge part of the fanbase.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T09:11:20-07:00","id":1514470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles#post1514463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys, I was reading about gargoyles in Requiem, and in Danse Macabre says the knowledge to create gargoyles is quite widespread, I founded it quite strange because the population of gargoyles shoulder be really higher (why trust just in ghouls to protect your haven if you can have a Gargoyles too). Did I missed something? Gargoyles never come up in games I played, so I wanted to know how usually things work in your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Basic knowledge&quot; of the Birthing Ritual is widely known, which is part of a sentence explaining why creating a gargoyle isn't something you need to belong to a specific covenant to learn how to do.<br /> <br /> Creating a gargoyle requires Blood Potency equal to twice the Rank of the gargoyle you're making and the upkeep cost is the gargoyle's Rank in Vitae per month, i.e. more than a ghoul's upkeep for most gargoyles.<br /> <br /> Most gargoyles are not very bright or self-motivated and can only perform basic tasks, whereas a ghoul is a person who can use their own intelligence and initiative. (Of the sample gargoyles, the only one with an Intelligence higher than 1 is a Size 1 messenger with Intelligence 2, built to carry confidential messages quickly.)<br /> <br /> <br /> None More Dark Publishing has made a Second Edition version of gargoyles in their 2e clanbook <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/395104/Wild-Hunt-Gangrel\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt: Gangrel</a> on the Storyteller's Vault; that version of the Birthing Ritual constitutes a Humanity 3 breaking point if successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T11:29:39-07:00","id":1514488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1514470#post1514470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Basic knowledge&quot; of the Birthing Ritual is widely known, which is part of a sentence explaining why creating a gargoyle isn't something you need to belong to a specific covenant to learn how to do.<br /> <br /> Creating a gargoyle requires Blood Potency equal to twice the Rank of the gargoyle you're making and the upkeep cost is the gargoyle's Rank in Vitae per month, i.e. more than a ghoul's upkeep for most gargoyles.<br /> <br /> Most gargoyles are not very bright or self-motivated and can only perform basic tasks, whereas a ghoul is a person who can use their own intelligence and initiative. (Of the sample gargoyles, the only one with an Intelligence higher than 1 is a Size 1 messenger with Intelligence 2, built to carry confidential messages quickly.)<br /> <br /> <br /> None More Dark Publishing has made a Second Edition version of gargoyles in their 2e clanbook <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/395104/Wild-Hunt-Gangrel\" target=\"_blank\">Wild Hunt: Gangrel</a> on the Storyteller's Vault; that version of the Birthing Ritual constitutes a Humanity 3 breaking point if successful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I started looking into Gargoyles because of Wild Hunt, I am a big fan of None More Dark work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I agree with all of your points, but the idea I got was more like wasn't that big of secret, but is strange for me gargoyles being kind common, so I my question is more like if should be common or if I am mistaken","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:39:46-07:00","id":1514514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1514488#post1514488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with all of your points, but the idea I got was more like wasn't that big of secret, but is strange for me gargoyles being kind common, so I my question is more like if should be common or if I am mistaken</div> </div> </div> </div>That's going to depend on how you intend to characterize the vampires of your chronicle's setting vis-a-vis how much blood they're willing to spill and what kind of problems they expect to need solutions for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T15:47:33-07:00","id":1514521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1514488#post1514488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I started looking into Gargoyles because of Wild Hunt, I am a big fan of None More Dark work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I agree with all of your points, but the idea I got was more like wasn't that big of secret, but is strange for me gargoyles being kind common, so I my question is more like if should be common or if I am mistaken</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as i tried to point out in my previous post (before the forums spam philter swallowed it) &quot;quite widespread&quot; is a very vague and loose definition that it can go from &quot;as common as ghouls&quot; (as you kind of compared them) to &quot;almost as numerous as users of Cruac, Theban Sorcery or Dragon's Coils&quot; to anywhere in between those extremes or beyond them, so it will strongly depend on ST and player preferences how commonplace or rare is their use.<br /> <br /> Last chronicle i played back in late 1st ed, we used the rules from Danse Macabre but with a tweak or two - Cruac or Theban Sorcery being added to Blood Potency to determine the maximum Rank of gargoyle a vampire might create, depending on certain merits and circunstances (Kindred with Of Rose of Thorn could add their level of Animalism instead if crafting gargoyles from plant matter) other disciplines might count too - meaning the access to the more powerful ones was somewhat less restricted than by RAW, but other limitations in upkeep, intelligence and etc as described by Satchel still applied.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T00:14:22-07:00","id":1514553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1514514#post1514514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's going to depend on how you intend to characterize the vampires of your chronicle's setting vis-a-vis how much blood they're willing to spill and what kind of problems they expect to need solutions for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, based upon Requiem's design, I guess this makes sense to be open ended. Just out of curiosity, how hard in your games usually is to get the knowledge on gargoyle creation? And how common they are?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T00:21:09-07:00","id":1514554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1514521#post1514521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, as i tried to point out in my previous post (before the forums spam philter swallowed it) &quot;quite widespread&quot; is a very vague and loose definition that it can go from &quot;as common as ghouls&quot; (as you kind of compared them) to &quot;almost as numerous as users of Cruac, Theban Sorcery or Dragon's Coils&quot; to anywhere in between those extremes or beyond them, so it will strongly depend on ST and player preferences how commonplace or rare is their use.<br /> <br /> Last chronicle i played back in late 1st ed, we used the rules from Danse Macabre but with a tweak or two - Cruac or Theban Sorcery being added to Blood Potency to determine the maximum Rank of gargoyle a vampire might create, depending on certain merits and circunstances (Kindred with Of Rose of Thorn could add their level of Animalism instead if crafting gargoyles from plant matter) other disciplines might count too - meaning the access to the more powerful ones was somewhat less restricted than by RAW, but other limitations in upkeep, intelligence and etc as described by Satchel still applied.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sounds really cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and makes sense to me. Actually originally I thought gargoyles was a product of blood sorcery, so that's is really flavourful for me.<br /> <br /> Following the same pattern as the message above, how you and your fellow players got the knowledge on gargoyle creation and how common was on the domain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T09:37:09-07:00","id":1514712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1514554#post1514554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's sounds really cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and makes sense to me. Actually originally I thought gargoyles was a product of blood sorcery, so that's is really flavourful for me.<br /> <br /> Following the same pattern as the message above, how you and your fellow players got the knowledge on gargoyle creation and how common was on the domain?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, that is a quite of convoluted story, to say the least - but it all starts with some mysterious event that <i>consumed</i> almost all kindred that were active in the domain in the early 18th century, leaving a city empty of any kindred that were not already in torpor and a number of bizarre beings and phenomena that are mostly gone, according to the words of the one lone kindred who dealt with the aftereffects of this unknown doom, the nosferatu <i>babalorix\u00e1</i>, an undead priest of the umbanda tradition, who would in later centuries become the local hierophant.<br /> <br /> Most of kindred were completely gone, never to be seen again, though a few would find ways to linger on, some by haunting torpid kindred with whom they had a blood sympathy or blood bond, specially after their awakening. But others through their own &quot;abandoned&quot; ghouls - human, animal and more - and a variety of strange puppet, statue or marionette things of their own creation. These partly possessed and empowered things would cause all kinds of little and not so little headaches for decades until the hierophant managed to subdue, contain them with the help of other kindred through the years, keeping these old, &quot;rogue&quot; gargoyles under his tutelage as watchers and keepsakes in his main sanctuary.<br /> <br /> In time he would also come to understand how to make his own, though considerably less independent or unruly, creations, knowledge that he passed to a few choice pupils through the decades and centuries. All of that said, according to his words when discussing the subject with my PC, he was also the first to admit that a few of the original &quot;freed&quot; gargoyles always eluded their grasp, or that some of the captured ones went rogue once again - and who knows which were really destroyed or captured for the personal study of a curious kindred or ghoul hunter instead.<br /> <br /> This would lead my character, a Gangrel Dragon with some peculiar gift to manipulate plants or hear and speak with the dead, to make some independent research and experimentation of his own, leading him to come in contact and exchange stories with a number of individual kindred or small groups across the domain, each familiar\u200b with how to create a certain type of Gargoyle or using some specific materials - a lone Carthian Toreador jeweler that discovered them on his own as a pastime to while away the nights, a synchretic underground &quot;church of Lilith&quot; that would be looked askance by followers of Longinus and Crone both if ever discovered, one or two disturbingly lifelike companions of the Invictus Primogen made in resemblance of his lost childer of yore through their inspiration, a secret cabal of rogue ghouls &amp; gargoyles doing bizarre routines and tasks to preserve their existences or in hope of bringing back their lost domitors and more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T09:02:25-07:00","id":1514848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1514712#post1514712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, that is a quite of convoluted story, to say the least - but it all starts with some mysterious event that <i>consumed</i> almost all kindred that were active in the domain in the early 18th century, leaving a city empty of any kindred that were not already in torpor and a number of bizarre beings and phenomena that are mostly gone, according to the words of the one lone kindred who dealt with the aftereffects of this unknown doom, the nosferatu <i>babalorix\u00e1</i>, an undead priest of the umbanda tradition, who would in later centuries become the local hierophant.<br /> <br /> Most of kindred were completely gone, never to be seen again, though a few would find ways to linger on, some by haunting torpid kindred with whom they had a blood sympathy or blood bond, specially after their awakening. But others through their own &quot;abandoned&quot; ghouls - human, animal and more - and a variety of strange puppet, statue or marionette things of their own creation. These partly possessed and empowered things would cause all kinds of little and not so little headaches for decades until the hierophant managed to subdue, contain them with the help of other kindred through the years, keeping these old, &quot;rogue&quot; gargoyles under his tutelage as watchers and keepsakes in his main sanctuary.<br /> <br /> In time he would also come to understand how to make his own, though considerably less independent or unruly, creations, knowledge that he passed to a few choice pupils through the decades and centuries. All of that said, according to his words when discussing the subject with my PC, he was also the first to admit that a few of the original &quot;freed&quot; gargoyles always eluded their grasp, or that some of the captured ones went rogue once again - and who knows which were really destroyed or captured for the personal study of a curious kindred or ghoul hunter instead.<br /> <br /> This would lead my character, a Gangrel Dragon with some peculiar gift to manipulate plants or hear and speak with the dead, to make some independent research and experimentation of his own, leading him to come in contact and exchange stories with a number of individual kindred or small groups across the domain, each familiar\u200b with how to create a certain type of Gargoyle or using some specific materials - a lone Carthian Toreador jeweler that discovered them on his own as a pastime to while away the nights, a synchretic underground &quot;church of Lilith&quot; that would be looked askance by followers of Longinus and Crone both if ever discovered, one or two disturbingly lifelike companions of the Invictus Primogen made in resemblance of his lost childer of yore through their inspiration, a secret cabal of rogue ghouls &amp; gargoyles doing bizarre routines and tasks to preserve their existences or in hope of bringing back their lost domitors and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sounds really cool, thank you for sharing! That gave me some ideas on how to introduce the gargoyle knowledge in game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T01:15:01-07:00","id":1517630,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this counts as thread necromancy or comes off as too much of a tangent, but reading this thread reminded me of why I fell in love with Requiem 1e way back when I was young.<br /> <br /> There was an open-ended weirdness within the whole World of Darkness at the time, especially when all you had were just the two core rulebooks and your own imagination, which was how my friends and I played for years. Gargoyles were a surprisingly common encounter in our games. None of us knew much about the original WoD setting from the 90's aside from the fact it existed at one point and so we didn't have nostalgia goggles on when we played Requiem for the first time (not yet at least, lol). We didn't get the chance to buy Werewolf or Mage back then, so we just made our own rules for lupines and magi because they were mentioned briefly in the core rules. Our group eventually got Hunter and Changeling and a few supplements like Armory and Nomads a couple years later, but that was it.<br /> <br /> Requiem 1e's corebook had weird stuff like Gargoyles, Homunculi, and Hellhounds that were never really brought up again until way later if they even got brought up again at all. A lot of people just forgot about them completely and some of that stuff didn't carry over into 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T14:38:25-07:00","id":1517824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1514463-gargoyles?p=1517630#post1517630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this counts as thread necromancy or comes off as too much of a tangent, but reading this thread reminded me of why I fell in love with Requiem 1e way back when I was young.<br /> <br /> There was an open-ended weirdness within the whole World of Darkness at the time, especially when all you had were just the two core rulebooks and your own imagination, which was how my friends and I played for years. Gargoyles were a surprisingly common encounter in our games. None of us knew much about the original WoD setting from the 90's aside from the fact it existed at one point and so we didn't have nostalgia goggles on when we played Requiem for the first time (not yet at least, lol). We didn't get the chance to buy Werewolf or Mage back then, so we just made our own rules for lupines and magi because they were mentioned briefly in the core rules. Our group eventually got Hunter and Changeling and a few supplements like Armory and Nomads a couple years later, but that was it.<br /> <br /> Requiem 1e's corebook had weird stuff like Gargoyles, Homunculi, and Hellhounds that were never really brought up again until way later if they even got brought up again at all. A lot of people just forgot about them completely and some of that stuff didn't carry over into 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really cool! World of Darkness and Vampire the Requiem books was my first contact with TTRPG. I take interest because of bloodlines, but at the time the newest game was Requiem, so I read it. And well I love masquerade, but I fell in love with Requiem. So I probably have a idea of the feeling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}